{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.StirlingRobbins","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StirlingRobbins","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Stirling"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.le_log_factorial_stirling_robbins","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.le_log_factorial_stirling_robbins","kind":"theorem","line":256,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StirlingRobbins.lean#L256-L283","doc":"**Robbins' bounds, both sides.**  For `n ≠ 0`,\n\n    n·log n − n + ½log n + ½log(2π) + 1/(12n+1)\n      ≤ log n! ≤\n    n·log n − n + ½log n + ½log(2π) + 1/(12n).\n\nThe lower bound strictly sharpens Mathlib's `Stirling.le_log_factorial_stirling`\n(which has no `1/(12n+1)` term), and the upper bound has no Mathlib counterpart\nat all.  Their gap is `1/(12n) − 1/(12n+1) = 1/(12n(12n+1)) = O(1/n²)`, which is\nwhat `qou-mlgp` (A) needs: the `−(π/12N)cot θ` refinement requires the `1/(12k)`\nterm to `o(1/N)` accuracy, and either bound alone leaves an `O(1/N)` hole. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.le_log_stirlingSeq_sub_log_sqrt_pi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.le_log_stirlingSeq_sub_log_sqrt_pi","kind":"theorem","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StirlingRobbins.lean#L226-L254","doc":"**`1/(12n+1) ≤ log σ(n) − log √π`** for `n ≠ 0` — Robbins' lower refinement,\nthe counterpart of `log_stirlingSeq_sub_log_sqrt_pi_le`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.log_stirlingSeq_sub_ge_robbins","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.log_stirlingSeq_sub_ge_robbins","kind":"theorem","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StirlingRobbins.lean#L214-L224","doc":"The telescoped lower bound over any range. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.log_stirlingSeq_diff_ge_robbins","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.log_stirlingSeq_diff_ge_robbins","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StirlingRobbins.lean#L192-L212","doc":"**The telescoping step, from below.**  The first term of the series already\ndominates `1/(12(m+1)+1) − 1/(12(m+2)+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.log_factorial_le_stirling_robbins","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.log_factorial_le_stirling_robbins","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StirlingRobbins.lean#L154-L177","doc":"**Robbins' upper bound.**  For `n ≠ 0`,\n\n    log n!  ≤  n·log n − n + ½·log n + ½·log(2π) + 1/(12n).\n\nThe exact counterpart of Mathlib's `Stirling.le_log_factorial_stirling`, with\nthe `1/(12n)` term its docstring records as missing.  Together the two pin\n`log n!` to within `1/(12n)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.log_stirlingSeq_sub_log_sqrt_pi_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.log_stirlingSeq_sub_log_sqrt_pi_le","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StirlingRobbins.lean#L133-L152","doc":"**`log σ(n) − log √π ≤ 1/(12n)`** for `n ≠ 0`, where `σ = stirlingSeq`.\n\nThe telescoping bound summed to infinity against `tendsto_stirlingSeq_sqrt_pi`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.log_stirlingSeq_sub_le_robbins","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.log_stirlingSeq_sub_le_robbins","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StirlingRobbins.lean#L120-L131","doc":"The telescoped bound over any range: `log σ(n+1) − log σ(m+1) ≤\n1/(12(n+1)) − 1/(12(m+1))` for `n ≤ m`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.log_stirlingSeq_diff_le_robbins","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.log_stirlingSeq_diff_le_robbins","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/StirlingRobbins.lean#L71-L118","doc":"**The telescoping bound.**  `log σ(n+1) − log σ(n+2) ≤ 1/(12(n+1)) − 1/(12(n+2))`.\n\nSharpening `Stirling.log_stirlingSeq_diff_le_geo_sum`, which bounds the series\ncoefficients `1/(2k+3)` by `1`.  Bounding them by `1/3` — their actual first\nvalue — turns the geometric sum into the telescoping difference exactly. ","signatureChunk":0}]}